  "_readme": [
    "Curated merchant identity. Keys and `canonical` values are merchantSlug() output (see lib/offers/merchants.ts).",
    "",
    "`canonical` MERGES two names into one merchant. Only ever use it for genuine spellings of ONE place a cardholder can walk into — 'pasikuda' / 'pasikudah' / 'passikuda' are the same resort. NEVER use it to fold siblings together: 'Jetwing Beach' and 'Jetwing Beach - The Deck' are a hotel and a restaurant inside it, and merging them would claim a dining discount covers a room booking. Two hotels in one chain are likewise two merchants.",
    "",
    "`group` is the soft relationship: same brand, still separate merchants. It powers a 'more from this brand' strip and never affects offer counts, bank counts, or the best-discount figure. Prefer it whenever you are tempted by `canonical` but not certain.",
    "",
    "Groups are curated rather than derived from the first word on purpose — 'Ceylon', 'Royal' and 'Colombo' each head a dozen unrelated businesses, and 'Layards Wharf' merely starts like 'Laya'.",
    "",
    "Regenerate candidates with: npx tsx scripts/merchant-fragmentation.ts"
  ],

